      "content": "That consistent scheduling pattern strongly suggests an automated routine rather than hacking or remote interference. You can check this by reviewing your Nest and Hue device history in the respective apps to see if the time dips align perfectly with a confirmed daily schedule. While you cannot easily view specific login locations on third-party accounts you don't own, you do have control over disc access and user groups to identify who made recent changes. Check for \"scheduled automation\" or \"voice routines\" in your settings immediately and create a temporary halt on all scheduling until you verify the source.",
